rc-plc/colorado/douglas-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 40 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair finished at 33% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 44% and June to July at 48% on the middle of the grids. Grid 22902 had its driest year in 2002 at 55%, and grid 23500 matched that 55% in 1954.</p>"}
